# Deliverable: 01-intake

This is the definition of done for the maker. It says what good looks like.
It does not say how the work is tested.

## Hand in

`brief.md`

## Format

Short headed sections, in this order: Type, Runbook id, Outcome, Trigger, Deliverables, Owner, Human yes points, Requires, Source (adoptions only), Open questions.

## Must be true

- Someone who never saw the request could author the runbook from this brief alone.
- Each deliverable is named, with who or what receives it.
- Human yes points are either listed, "none", or "undecided". "None" is only used when a person decided it.

## Out of scope

- Writing stage instructions or QA criteria.
- Improving an adopted process.
